# Zone 1, room 1 (grey box, Phase 1 task 7): tech 1, dash-slash.
# BUILD.md s5, tech 1: "Dash into attack, frame-perfect cancel. Taught by a tight corridor of weak
# enemies"; s5 Dash: "cancelable into attack from frame 6"; s6 Taper (side 1: 10 damage, box 68 x 44 u).
#
# Layout: the west hall (25 tiles) with one dummy standing still (the safe first encounter: nothing
# swings, one slash kills it, it comes back 60 ticks later), then a corridor 41 tiles (1312 u) long
# and 2 tiles (64 u) high, then the east hall. The corridor is as low as a dummy is tall, so there
# is no jumping over them: the standing body (44 u) has 20 u above its head, and a swing's box
# (64 u long, 48 u tall) fills the corridor in front of the dummy.
# Stand-ins: the weak enemies are 12 training dummies (hp 10: one side slash kills one), 96 u apart
# from x 880 to 1936, all swinging in step (marker `attack=1 period=30`: a white swing every 78
# ticks, 24 telegraph, 4 active, 20 recovery, then 30 idle). A dummy has no body to stop the player
# (enemy collision is not built yet), so the room cannot force the tech: it makes it clearly the
# best way across, measured in tests/replay/zone1/01_*:
#   dash-slash chain (a dash, a slash on its frame 6, a dash again as the ground cooldown allows): 242 ticks to the
#     east door, no hit taken (5 hearts);
#   running slashes (a slash every 12 ticks, the best a plain attacker does): 309 ticks (67 more),
#     and a hit lands if the pace slips (zone1_01_control_run_slashes);
#   running through without slashing: 329 ticks and two hits (zone1_01_control_run).
# Why it wins: the dash is 20 u/f for 9 frames (invulnerable on frames 1 to 7) against the run's
# 9 u/f, and the slash on frame 6 clears the dummy in the way without stopping.
room zone1/01_dash_slash
size 80 34
spawn 96 832
tiles
